  "name": "Warao song (Orinoco delta shamanic song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Warao of the Orinoco delta sing for curing, ritual and daily life, and their shamans, the wisiratu, hoarotu and bahanarotu, sing long healing and invocation songs, the wisiratu shaking a large sacred gourd rattle. Other repertories use the isimoi clarinet of the nahanamu festival, bone and cane flutes and the sekeseke violin. Dale A. Olsen recorded Warao music in the 1970s for the Folkways album Music of the Warao of Venezuela. The shaker card stands in for the shaman's gourd rattle.",
